From: ROCKNIX <devnull@rocknix.org>
Subject: [PATCH] mali: allow shared regulators to remain above the GPU OPP

RK3326 supplies the GPU and DMC from the same vdd_logic regulator.  An
exact GPU voltage request conflicts with a higher DMC voltage request and
causes either device's devfreq transition to fail with -EINVAL.

Follow the Rockchip BSP Mali driver and express the GPU OPP voltage as a
minimum requirement.  The regulator core can then select the highest
minimum requested by all consumers of the shared rail.

--- a/product/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c
+++ b/product/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/backend/gpu/mali_kbase_devfreq.c
@@ -166,7 +166,7 @@ static int kbase_devfreq_target(struct device *dev, unsigned long *target_freq,
 	for (i = 0; i < kbdev->nr_clocks; i++) {
 		if (kbdev->regulators[i] && kbdev->current_voltages[i] != volts[i] &&
 		    kbdev->current_freqs[i] < freqs[i]) {
-			err = regulator_set_voltage(kbdev->regulators[i], volts[i], volts[i]);
+			err = regulator_set_voltage(kbdev->regulators[i], volts[i], INT_MAX);
 			if (!err) {
 				kbdev->current_voltages[i] = volts[i];
 			} else {
@@ -200,7 +200,7 @@ static int kbase_devfreq_target(struct device *dev, unsigned long *target_freq,
 	for (i = 0; i < kbdev->nr_clocks; i++) {
 		if (kbdev->regulators[i] && kbdev->current_voltages[i] != volts[i] &&
 		    original_freqs[i] > freqs[i]) {
-			err = regulator_set_voltage(kbdev->regulators[i], volts[i], volts[i]);
+			err = regulator_set_voltage(kbdev->regulators[i], volts[i], INT_MAX);
 			if (!err) {
 				kbdev->current_voltages[i] = volts[i];
 			} else {
